    "explanation": "To both parties. The GPS trace for TRP-02804 governs the distance (POL-RD-01): it measures 29.13 km against the booked optimal of 22.1 km, an excess of 7.03 km, or 31.81%. That clears both establishment gates (above 20% and above 0.8 km). The trip record's 29.1 km is a rounded convenience copy and was not used for the threshold. The excess is below both materiality gates (50% and 8.0 km), so this is an ordinary established deviation and POL-RD-06 is not engaged. The rider's two POL-RD-06 concessions and the driver's are accepted: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 329 completed trips in 90 days, far below the pattern test, so there is no full-refund uplift and no driver-conduct referral, and prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter that POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting. For the rider: the fare is METERED, so the remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. Charged_total 45.82 less a recomputed fare of 36.7628 — (3.80 + 0.75 x 22.1 + 0.28 x 29.8) x the 1.2 surge multiplier read from EV-FARE-02804, plus the 0.80 platform fee and the 1.50 on-optimal-route ERP — leaves 9.0572, rounded up to SGD 9.10. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and is 19.77% of the amount charged, far below the 90% that would make it a full refund; the SGD 8.50 you contested is recovered in full. For the driver: your statement that traffic was heavy and you took another road cites no evidence ID; under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and is discarded, and the traffic_advisory for this trip (EV-ADVIS-02804-01) is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run on this record and your excuse neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. Your advocate's argument that citing that missing identifier forces escalation under POL-RD-10(5) is rejected: the asserting party here is you, and your own statement names no advisory ID. POL-RD-13(1) applies — the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against an artifact you cited — so the deviation stands at the measured figure and no escalation follows. Pass-through: the single ERP line, PIE Eunos westbound SGD 1.50, is on the optimal route and the trace passes 35.3 m from the gantry, inside the 250 m crossing radius, so it is properly chargeable and is already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 recomputation; POL-RD-09(1) forbids adding it on top, and no billing-integrity referral arises. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes — 229 fixes at a 10.0 s interval, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0 — so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged, the trip identifiers and timestamps agree, and no other POL-RD-10 trigger fires. Every exculpatory route is closed on the record: the chat log is empty (POL-RD-04), no amendment was made (POL-RD-05, amended fields null), and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12). The monetary effect of SGD 9.10 exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this provisional ruling issues but is not executed automatically; the amount is held and the case goes to the human queue for release. Confidence 0.90, capped at 1.0 by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts (EV-GPS-02804, EV-TRIP-02804, EV-FARE-02804)."
